WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.467
-I don't know how to sit.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.634
-You did a great job.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.300
You always overthink it.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.701
Did you overthink
sitting right now?

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.100
-Well, you know,
like when you're,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.200
I don't know, filming anything
and they're like,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.934
talk on the phone,
but make it look natural

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.067
and then you don't because
you're overthinking it.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.834
-Yeah
-I just overthought sitting.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.267
-Yeah.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.901
You look pretty good sitting.
-Thanks, man.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:19.968
-It looks like
you've done it before.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.701
-I watched.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.167
-You've researched a lot
of tape and stuff and stuff.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.634
-Lot of years of sitting.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.901
-You're one of the best sitters
I've ever sat next to.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:29.667
-I appreciate that.
-You're welcome, yeah.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.501
-This is your talk show debut.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.200
-Yes, sir. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.033
-I'm honored.
I'm honored that you're here.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.267
-It's an honor to be here.
-Welcome.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.934
-Yeah, first of many times.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.033
You're in one of the biggest
shows in the world right now.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.367
"The Night Agent."

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.634
People can't
stop talking about this,

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.968
but there's another role
that you played

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:47.667
that people can't stop
talking about.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:48.968
And if you know
what I'm talking about,

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:52.834
But you were once
on the show "iCarly."

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.434
-Yeah.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.400
-Is that you?
-That is me.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.501
-Yeah.
-It's hard to tell.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:00:59.868
-Yeah, yeah.
-I think the whole premise

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.267
of the show
is it was hard to tell.

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.734
Yeah. What was it, like,
a bizarro world or what was it?

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.133
Like, You played Freddy.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.601
-So I had my own idea
of what should have happened

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:12.667
where there's like a battle
for who gets to be Freddy,

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:15.467
you know, and the fakes
try to remove the real ones.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.067
But they didn't like that.
It's Nickelodeon.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.901
-Yeah, I know.
Of course, yeah.

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:22.200
What do you remember
about doing it?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.000
-I don't remember much,
to be honest.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.033
I forgot that this happened
until recently,

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.467
and everyone was reminding
me of it.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.834
-Because the Internet
just loves it.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.701
-Yeah. So I don't remember.
-You don't remember?

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.200
-It was fun, I guess,
as a kid.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.634
-Yeah. And now it's having
a resurgence.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.567
-Yeah.
-How long have you been acting?

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.934
Since how old?
How young were you?

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:41.901
-13 to 18,
and then I quit

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.567
for like seven or eight years.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.234
-And you quit
because you just go

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.634
it's -- I don't feel like it,

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:47.934
it's not for me
right now or...?

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.901
-I just...

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:53.467
I think actors are really
insulated from reality.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.801
And I think of all people,

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.067
actors should be the least
insulated people

00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:00.200
because they got to, like,
portray real things.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.334
And so everything sort of felt
like a pseudo experience to me,

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:07.067
like, as a kid where,
oh, you can be the fighter

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.701
And then not actually
hit anybody

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.434
or know what it's like
to get hit or whatever.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:12.968
It just felt very fake.

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:15.133
So I quit because I was --

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.300
I didn't want to be depressed.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.400
-Good, good.
Good luck, buddy.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.968
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:22.968
-And now I'm back.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:25.033
-Yeah, now you're back.
Yeah.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:27.467
You got a smile on your face.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:28.701
-Yeah.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.901
-But you can do so many things.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:37.000
I was looking on the Internet

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.000
about the different skills
that you --

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.267
-I hope it was on
the Internet,

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.100
and you're weren't,
like, watching.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.601
-I wanted -- Yeah, I'm --
I'm watching every move.

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:47.767
Yeah, but you can
you're -- you're skilled

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.968
at knife throwing,
archery, weightlifting,

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:52.834
professional fighting, drums...

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:53.901
-Amateur fighting, yeah.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.200
-Yeah. Sorry.
I aided professional.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.067
-I don't get paid.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:01.634
-Drums, violin,
drawing, welding.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:04.167
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.734
It's fantastic.
-I don't have a social life.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.434
-Yeah, no.
But, I mean,

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:13.000
this is one of the other
things you just, I guess...

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.434
Did you just get a Master?
What do you get?

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.701
-Oh. So, yeah.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.434
I got my DSWA
walling license,

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.634
so that's dry stone.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.434
I'm a stonemason.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.968
-So, you know, how --
how did you...

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.067
-So I have a trade.
I'm useful.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.334
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.501
Yes, you are useful.

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.667
Yes.
-Yes.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.100
-You are useful.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.467
But this is beautiful.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.334
This is --
I'm so jealous of this.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.400
I couldn't do anything
like this.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.434
I couldn't do.
That's a gorgeous wall.

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:44.801
And when someone builds someone
a wall, it better be good

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.868
because it has to stand
the test of time.

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:47.934
-Yeah, I hope it does.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.367
And that's sort of
the funny thing

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:51.400
is you're building
these things that, I don't know,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.767
kind of put this business
in context because you're like

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:56.934
this will last way longer
than people --

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.434
than my show will last.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:03:59.834
And then you go outside

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.534
and you're looking
at your wall...

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:07.567
It's not really funny.
It's just sort of like --

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.734
-I think, again, you're being
a little hard on yourself.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.100
-I think it's a good thing

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.701
because I think people
have so much ego about stuff

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.601
and to look at a wall
and be like,

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:22.100
wow, if they lost their Wi-Fi,
they couldn't watch my show.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.300
But this wall, like,
serves a purpose

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.934
and will be around.

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.167
It just...

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.634
[ Laughs ]

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.801
Dude, you're...

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:34.634
You have to come back
on the show.

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.601
You're one of my favorite
guests we've ever had.

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:39.501
You're fascinating to me.
I agree with you.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:42.167
That wall will last for...

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:45.200
-It should.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.634
-I don't know.
-No, I --

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:49.901
I think you got something.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.033
Let's talk about
"The Night Agent,"

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.667
because this is --
it already got picked up

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:55.067
for another season.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.067
-We're still on one.
-Well done.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.767
-Thank you.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:00.300
Thank you.
-How does it feel?

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.534
Because I know you do the show,
you work hard on it,

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:05.701
and then it comes out and then
everyone's watching and you go,

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.767
"Oh, this is kind of cool.
People are talking about this.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.267
I didn't know who would, like,
if it would catch on

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.033
or be as big as..."
It's giant.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:15.767
-It's always nice
when people enjoy things,

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:17.901
but especially
when it's like your art.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:20.634
But for me,
it's a little uncomfortable

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.133
because I do pen
and ink illustrations

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.200
and stuff and, like,
that's me.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.300
That's from my head.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.534
This is so, like,
collaborative.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:32.834
And when you're done
and you're working, you're done.

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:35.667
And then everything that happens
that everyone else sees

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:38.133
was so out of your control
and out of your hands

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:41.601
that it's sort of like people
compliment you

00:05:41.601 --> 00:05:44.100
because society sees it's you,
but then you're like,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.601
but I didn't edit
the stuff.

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:50.501
I didn't -- I didn't do anything
other than my job.

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:55.200
So it's, like, it's just
uncomfortable for me.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.300
Like --
-This is the realest interview

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.767
I've ever had in my life.

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:03.100
It's unbelievable, fascinating.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:07.133
-I remember I had
a camera operator.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.300
-Just keep going.
Keep going.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.033
-There was a camera operator
buddy of mine.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.000
-Tell me about it.
-And I just...

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.968
-I think this is --
-I have a good --

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:22.100
I have a good fix for you.
-You do?

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.501
-Yeah, let me
fix you real quick.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.200
-You have a -- you have
a good fix for me.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.634
But -- so you have...

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.000
-So, -I'm looking at the camera
operator and I'm like,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.133
wow, this job does not happen
without a camera operator.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:35.467
And in the same way, it doesn't
happen without a focus puller.

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:39.100
So it's like we're all
sort of working together,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.968
and then the end product
though,

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.567
everybody's like, "Gabe,
we love you."

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.534
And I'm like --
-It's a team.

00:06:44.534 --> 00:06:45.868
-Yeah, it's a team thing.

00:06:45.868 --> 00:06:48.701
It's like on a ship -- and this
is how I think about it.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:52.534
If it's a ship,
like those old Greek ships

00:06:52.534 --> 00:06:54.133
and everybody
has an oar in the water,

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:57.400
like I have my oar
and I'm doing my job.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.934
And as long as I don't screw up,

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:03.067
the boat's going to get
where it needs to go.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:05.968
But we all have to orient
to the captain's authority.

00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:08.634
And it's not like --
if you have ego,

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:10.701
then it's like the ship
doesn't go anywhere

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:11.767
because it's not my job.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.267
-Well, you make a turn
in the one way

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:14.901
because you're rowing
too hard on that side.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:16.767
-You get frustrated because
you're the, you know,

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:18.868
the guy and you take your oar
out of the water

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:20.300
and then it's this
self-fulfilling, like...

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.133
-Yeah, and then I see you,
I nudge you, I go,

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:23.767
"Look, he's not even rowing."

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:24.934
-Yeah, exactly.

00:07:24.934 --> 00:07:26.167
And the captain's like,
"What the hell?"

00:07:26.167 --> 00:07:27.701
And you're like, "Well..."

00:07:27.701 --> 00:07:28.701
-Talk to Larry.
-Yeah.

00:07:28.701 --> 00:07:30.501
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:32.067
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:33.067
Here's...

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:35.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:37.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:39.968
Gabriel Basso.

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:42.701
-Gabriel Basso in
"The Night Agent."

00:07:42.701 --> 00:07:44.167
Take a look at this.

00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:49.200
♪♪

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:56.534
♪♪

00:07:56.534 --> 00:07:58.000
-Guys, I think
I see a way down.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.267
Come on.
Take my hand.

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:01.234
-Okay.
-Come on.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.033
-Oh, my God!

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.567
-[ Groans, coughs ]

00:08:07.567 --> 00:08:09.767
-Are you okay?

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:12.067
Peter?

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:14.067
-Your turn.
-I'm not jumping down there.

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:15.634
-I'll catch you.
-You'll catch me?

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:17.033
-Yes.
-That's crazy.

00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:18.934
-Crazier than waiting around
for your friend? Come on.

00:08:18.934 --> 00:08:22.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:22.567 --> 00:08:24.300
-Gabriel Basso.
-What clip was that?

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.801
-I quickly wanted to show
what an amazing

00:08:28.801 --> 00:08:31.234
artist you are with
pen and ink there.

00:08:31.234 --> 00:08:32.567
This is a picture of you.
-Cant' really tell.

00:08:32.567 --> 00:08:34.901
-It's a dark photo,
but this -- you --

00:08:34.901 --> 00:08:36.133
That looks like Keanu Reeves.

00:08:36.133 --> 00:08:38.133
-Yeah.
-Is it?

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:42.801
-Yeah. He -- he commissioned
a piece for me, and I...

00:08:42.801 --> 00:08:44.033
-That is Keanu Reeves.
-Yeah.

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:45.667
-Hey, cool.
-What's funny about

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:48.000
this picture too,
is like the context of,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.868
Hey, you do pen and ink art
and you can't even see the art.

00:08:49.868 --> 00:08:51.334
And it's like, That's Keanu.

00:08:51.334 --> 00:08:53.234
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:55.067
Yeah, so...

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:57.300
[ Applause ]

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.667
-Get out of here.

00:08:58.667 --> 00:09:00.734
[ Laughs ]

00:09:00.734 --> 00:09:02.868
Can you come back
on the show Monday?

00:09:02.868 --> 00:09:04.934
I want to keep
talking to you.

00:09:04.934 --> 00:09:05.934
You're fascinating.
You'll work it out.

00:09:05.934 --> 00:09:07.267
-You have my number.
-Yeah.

00:09:07.267 --> 00:09:09.334
-Thank you very much.
Gabriel Basso.

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:12.701
"The Night Agent" is streaming
now on Netflix.

00:09:12.701 --> 00:09:14.367
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:09:14.367 --> 00:09:15.667
Stick around, everybody.

